label: Fetch Proxied
description: >-
  Query a county FeatureServer THROUGH app.fetchgis.com. The PIN is disclosed
  to the proxy operator; for corridor queries the full buffer geometry is too.

  Corresponds to `fetchParcel` in iosco.ts / otsego.ts, which build
  `${PROXY}proxy.ashx?${encodeURIComponent(targetUrl)}` and send a spoofed
  Referer header.

  Note the output: `sourceTrust: aggregator`, not `verified`. blue-ribbon does
  not currently make that distinction -- OPEN_ITEMS.md:143-146 worries about
  "depending on a re-aggregator rather than the county's own authoritative
  source, a different trust posture than every other adapter", but that worry
  lives in a markdown file and nothing in the code acts on it. Here it is the
  node's declared output, and it propagates through combineProvenance
  automatically.

  THIS IS THE STRONGEST ARGUMENT FOR WEIR IN THE WHOLE EXERCISE. A concern
  that was prose became a value that flows.
effect: http
input: ProxiedCountyQuery
output: RawParcelFeature
examples:
  - given:
      ProxiedCountyQuery:
        pin: "062-026-300-020-00"
        county: "Iosco"
        endpoint: "https://services3.arcgis.com/iosco/FeatureServer/0/query"
        proxyHost: "app.fetchgis.com"
        referer: "https://app.fetchgis.com/?currentMap=iosco"
    expect:
      RawParcelFeature:
        county: "Iosco"
        sourceTrust: "aggregator"
        featureJson: '{"properties":{"TaxID":"062-026-300-020-00","Shape_Area":370701.0},"geometry":{"type":"Polygon","coordinates":[[[-83.4,44.4],[-83.4,44.5],[-83.3,44.5],[-83.4,44.4]]]}}'
